The ranking seam `tm-oracle plan` grafts onto fork 4748911 (stage 6 W-39 track H;
the owner's D72, README gap 3533).  `build-oracle.sh` applies it with `git apply`
to the extracted fork and FAILS the build when it does not apply, so the oracle
never runs a planner this file does not describe.

Fork 4748911's `planner::plan` takes no priorities: its `PlanInput` has no ranking
and its step 4 always runs the fork's own §7 pass (`priority::compute`) over its own
lookahead.  The shipped binary has fed the fork the KERNEL's ranking since `09d38fa`
(stage 5 D10 L8, "every priority comes from the kernel"), and that commit made
exactly two edits to what the fork's day planning reads, both reproduced here and
nothing else:

  1. the ranking seam — `PlanInput::prios` and `PlanInput::with_ranking`, step 4
     reading the given priorities (restricted to the candidates §9.1's overrides
     keep) instead of running the fork's own pass;
  2. §7.3's IMPOSSIBLE reading the EXACT shortfall — `09d38fa` made
     `Prio::is_impossible` read the exact shortfall's numerator, so a shortfall of
     a fraction of a minute is impossible though its floor is 0; here one bit per
     priority, whether the exact shortfall is positive, carried with each grant
     the kernel ranked (false on every priority the fork computes, whose shortfall
     is whole minutes).

`09d38fa`'s other planner edits (the week plan's capacity in exact units, the
`caps` it carries) plan no day, and are left out.

